(AI & MACHINE LEARNING PRIMER: FOUNDATIONS) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Chapter 1: Supervised vs Unsupervised Learning) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Machine learning systems fall into three primary algorithmic paradigms:) Tj
T* (1. Supervised Learning: Models infer a function from labeled training data containing) Tj
T* (   input vectors X and target labels Y. Key applications include binary classification) Tj
T* (   \(e.g., medical diagnostics\) and continuous regression \(e.g., house price forecasting\).) Tj
T* (2. Unsupervised Learning: Discovers latent patterns, cluster boundaries, or low-dimensional) Tj
T* (   representations in unlabeled data. Notable algorithms include K-Means clustering,) Tj
T* (   Principal Component Analysis \(PCA\), and autoencoders.) Tj
T* (3. Reinforcement Learning: Agents optimize decision policies through environmental) Tj
T* (   rewards and penalties within a Markov Decision Process \(MDP\) setting.) Tj
ET
endstream
