(ARTIFICIAL NEURAL NETWORKS & BACKPROPAGATION) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Chapter 2: Deep Architectures, Activation Functions, and Optimization) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Artificial neural networks consist of stacked layers of parameterized units:) Tj
T* (- Rectified Linear Unit \(ReLU\): Defined as f\(x\) = max\(0, x\). Solves vanishing gradient) Tj
T* (  problems across deep architectures and offers high computational efficiency.) Tj
T* (- Sigmoid: Squashes input to the range \(0, 1\), standard for binary classification heads.) Tj
T* (- Softmax: Normalizes real-valued logits into a categorical probability distribution) Tj
T* (  summing to 1.0, essential for multi-class classification.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Backpropagation computes the exact analytical gradients of the loss function with) Tj
T* (respect to network weights by recursively applying the chain rule from the final layer) Tj
T* (backwards to input layers.) Tj
ET
endstream
