(GENERALIZATION, OVERFITTING & REGULARIZATION) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Chapter 3: Mitigating Variance and Improving Generalization) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Overfitting occurs when a high-capacity model fits random noise in the training set,) Tj
T* (producing poor validation accuracy. Established regularization strategies include:) Tj
T* (1. L1 Regularization \(Lasso\): Adds the absolute sum of weights to loss, enforcing) Tj
T* (   parameter sparsity and serving as implicit feature selection.) Tj
T* (2. L2 Regularization \(Ridge / Weight Decay\): Penalizes squared weights, ensuring) Tj
T* (   smooth parameter distributions without extreme weight magnitudes.) Tj
T* (3. Dropout: Randomly zeros out hidden unit activations during forward training passes) Tj
T* (   with probability p, breaking co-adaptation between feature detectors.) Tj
T* (4. Early Stopping: Monitors validation error and terminates training when loss) Tj
T* (   consistently increases, preventing over-training.) Tj
ET
endstream
